<title>UK: Iran buys cargoes of raw, white sugar -traders.</title>
<headline>Iran buys cargoes of raw, white sugar -traders.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Iran bought 30,000 tonnes of raw sugar for March/May shipment and 14,000 tonnes of white sugar for April, London traders said on Friday.</p>
<p>Prices paid were $269.00 per tonne for the raws and $313.00 for the whites, they added. Details of the suppliers have yet to emerge.</p>
<p>Earlier this month, Iran bought two 15,000-tonne cargoes of Cuban raw sugar from a London-based house at $257.00 and $258.00 per tonne for March/April shipment.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8064</p>
